# ===== A. macOS / external-disk environment noise (the repo lives on a working disk = a USB/external volume; not one safety rule may be dropped) =====
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100/
.fseventsd
.Trashes/
.Trash-*
.DocumentRevisions-V100/
.TemporaryItems/
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
.amelioration/
.ameliorating*
com.apple.*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.task_state/


# ===== B. .hermes relay layer = the whole directory stays out of version control (one big-hammer rule) =====
# YC ruling of 2026-10-10, translated: "anything inside .hermes stays out of version control" -- this supersedes the six-B whitelist negate structure approved by PM under r9.
# contracts/, assets/ui-reference/, reports/, build-smoke/, scratch/ all physically exist inside the repo (on the working disk, travels with the disk, auditable) but are not tracked by git;
# the File-as-Contract carrier is the repo directory entity (not the version chain). The former B.3 argument section is archived (see the six-B B.3 annotation).
.hermes/

# ===== C. UxPlay runtime artifacts (project-specific trap; keeps identity material and dumps from landing in cwd) =====
*.pem
*.key
.uxplay.pem
.uxplay.register
.uxplay.dacp
/audiodump*
/videodump*
*.h264
*.aud
*.alac
*.mp4
*.log

# ===== D. Build artifacts (both J2 legs alike; source bodies DO enter git -- see group F, do not conflate) =====
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcscmblueprint
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
build/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
*.o
*.a
*.dylib
*.so
*.app/
*.dSYM/
*.linkmap
# packaging/ = the default output root of scripts/build/package-release.sh: rebuildable build artifacts
# (~192 MB, incl. the E8 final package), excluded per BLUEPRINT.md:503 group F "build artifacts do not
# enter version control". The physical files stay on disk for sha256 re-verification.
packaging/

# scripts/build/ = a tracked SOURCE directory (group A6), not a build-artifact directory; re-included here
# because the build/ rule above would otherwise shadow it (git: the later rule wins).
!/scripts/build/

# ===== D2. UxPlay upstream source tree (2026-10-19 decouple: now produced by scripts/build/vendor-uxplay.sh, out of version control) =====
# core/uxplay/ used to be the vendored upstream source body (the GPL Corresponding Source). Since 2026-10-19 it is
# materialized by scripts/build/vendor-uxplay.sh from the fork (pins in core/vendor.lock) into
# _build/uxplay; this path keeps only a backward-compatible ignore rule, and any leftover files must never re-enter version control.
/core/uxplay/

# ===== E. Editor / shell miscellany =====
*.swp
*~
.Idea/
.vscode/

# ===== F. Positive declaration (these paths are hit by none of the rules above = tracked by default; pinned here so a later ignore line cannot swallow them) =====
# core/uxplay/**            upstream UxPlay source body (the GPL derivative work itself = the duty to convey Corresponding Source).
#                           since 2026-10-19 obtained from the fork via scripts/build/vendor-uxplay.sh (see core/vendor.lock
#                           repo/branch/commit/tree/manifest pins), materialized into _build/uxplay
#                           (the whole _build tree is excluded by group G); this path is ignored by group D2 and no longer enters version control.
#                           corresponding-source reproducibility = scripts/build/vendor-uxplay.sh + core/vendor.lock + manifest.
# app/Package.resolved      SwiftPM resolution pin = the Swift-side ledger twin of deps.lock; it must enter the version chain
# LICENSE / README.md / CONTRIBUTING.md / deps.lock / scripts/** / app/** / core/bridge/** / core/spawn/**

# ===== G. Build output root =====
# _build/ holds every generated artifact: the cmake cache and core build (<root>/core), the
# materialized upstream source tree (<root>/uxplay), the SwiftPM cache (<root>/app.swiftpm), the
# GStreamer closure cache (<root>/closure) and the assembled bundle (<root>/MiragePlay.app).
# One root rule is required, not optional: group D's patterns only cover file types (*.o/*.a/
# *.app/CMakeCache.txt), while `core/uxplay`, `app.swiftpm/<triple>/debug/MiragePlay`,
# `app-build-meta.env` and the vendored *.c/*.cpp bodies carry no such extension. Without this
# line they appear in `git status --porcelain` and build-app.sh --release refuses to ship.
/_build/
